## NOTEBOOKLM PROMPTS FOR PYQ ANALYSIS

Use these prompts in your NotebookLM notebook (which has all 483 PW PYQ files loaded):

**Prompt 1 — Frequency analysis:**
```
From all the NEET PYQ papers in this notebook (2015-2025), which topics appear most frequently?
List the top 20 topics by number of appearances across all years.
Include: topic name, chapter, subject, approximate frequency per year.
```

**Prompt 2 — Chapter-wise deep dive:**
```
From the CHAPTERWISE PYQ folder, analyze questions from the chapter "[CHAPTER NAME]".
What are the most common question types? What specific facts/formulas are tested?
What are the exact tricky points that appear as distractors?
```

**Prompt 3 — Trend analysis:**
```
Comparing NEET 2020-2022 vs 2023-2025 papers in this notebook:
Which topics have increased in frequency? Which have decreased?
What is the overall trend in difficulty level? Are there more application-based questions now?
```

**Prompt 4 — Prediction:**
```
Based on all NEET papers from 2015-2025 in this notebook:
If NEET 2026 follows past patterns, which 10 Biology topics are most likely to appear?
Which 5 Physics chapters guarantee the most questions?
Which Chemistry topics appear every single year without fail?
```

